<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/coast-breach.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/coast-breach-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/coast-breach.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.12"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/claim-toolbox/">Claim toolbox</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Hurricane Deductible Calculator</span></nav><p class="tag">Free calculator · runs in your browser</p><h1>Hurricane and Windstorm Deductible Calculator</h1><p class="lede">A 2% hurricane deductible on a $465,000 home is $9,300, not $1,000. See your deductible in real dollars and compare what a claim pays when the hurricane trigger is met and when it isn’t.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv">
<div class="tool" data-tool="deduct">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Hurricane &amp; windstorm deductible calculator</span><i>Percentage vs. flat</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <div><label for="w-a">Dwelling coverage (Coverage A)</label><input id="w-a" name="cova" inputmode="decimal" value="465000"><span class="hint">From your declarations page.</span></div>
      <div class="row2">
        <div><label for="w-p">Hurricane / windstorm deductible</label><select id="w-p" name="pct"><option value="1">1%</option><option value="2" selected>2%</option><option value="3">3%</option><option value="5">5%</option><option value="10">10%</option></select></div>
        <div><label for="w-min">Minimum dollar amount (if any)</label><input id="w-min" name="min" inputmode="decimal" value="2500"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="row2">
        <div><label for="w-f">All-other-perils deductible</label><input id="w-f" name="flat" inputmode="decimal" value="1000"></div>
        <div><label for="w-l">Estimated storm damage</label><input id="w-l" name="loss" inputmode="decimal" value="27800"></div>
      </div>
      <fieldset class="plain"><legend>Does the hurricane deductible apply to this storm?</legend>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <label class="check"><input type="radio" name="trig" value="yes" checked> <span>Yes, the trigger was met</span></label>
          <label class="check"><input type="radio" name="trig" value="no"> <span>No, it was a nor’easter or the trigger wasn’t met</span></label>
        </div></fieldset>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="out-big"><small>Deductible that applies</small><b data-o="pd">$0</b></div>
      <div class="stack" aria-hidden="true"><span class="s-c"></span><span class="s-a"></span></div>
      <div class="legend"><span><i class="s-c"></i>You pay</span><span><i class="s-a"></i>Policy pays</span></div>
      <div class="out-rows">
        <div><span>Hurricane deductible in dollars</span><b data-o="hd">$0</b></div>
        <div><span>Payment with hurricane deductible</span><b data-o="pdpay">$0</b></div>
        <div><span>Payment with the flat deductible</span><b data-o="flatpay">$0</b></div>
        <div><span>Difference the trigger makes</span><b data-o="diff">$0</b></div>
      </div>
      <p class="out-msg" data-o="below"></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></div>
<p class="hint tool-hint">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice, and nothing you type is stored.</p></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>Why the trigger matters in New Jersey</h2>
<p>Hurricane deductibles usually apply only when the policy’s trigger language is met, for example a hurricane warning issued for New Jersey or a storm officially classed as a hurricane. After Superstorm Sandy in 2012, the state said hurricane deductibles should not apply because Sandy wasn’t a hurricane when it came ashore. Nor’easters usually fall under the ordinary deductible unless your policy uses a broader windstorm deductible.</p>
<h2>Where to find yours</h2>
<p>Look on the declarations page for “hurricane,” “windstorm” or “named storm” deductible, then find the endorsement that defines it. Note any minimum dollar amount.</p>
<h2>What it means for appraisal</h2>
<p>The deductible doesn’t change the amount of loss a panel decides. It changes what you receive. A loss just above the deductible may not be worth disputing. One far above it may be.</p>
<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Does the percentage apply to my contents too?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="ans"><p>The percentage is usually calculated from the dwelling limit and then applied to the whole storm loss. Check your policy’s wording.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I lower my hurricane deductible?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="ans"><p>Sometimes, at renewal, for a higher premium. Coastal homes may have fewer options.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free tools</h2><div class="related"><a class="rel" href="/claim-toolbox/claim-calendar-builder/"><small>Planner</small>Claim Calendar Builder<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/claim-toolbox/appraisal-readiness-checkup/"><small>Checklist</small>Appraisal Readiness Checkup<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/claim-toolbox/fallen-tree-coverage-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small>Fallen Tree Coverage Calculator<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/>